30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms are worrying. Nine out of fourteen said they wouldn't commit to a whole year at once.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The ledger confirms our fixed costs are high. But the treasurer's logs show chasing individual payments is a nightmare.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sign-in tally is stark. A quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never show up.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The mid-year joiners needed hand-worked calculations. That is why they hesitate. It feels like a hassle.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The bank statements show a third of renewals needed reminders. We are bleeding cash flow.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if chasing payments takes six hours a month, a flat fee might be the only way to save the treasurer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, yes. But if we go flat, the non-attendees feel they are subsidizing the active ones.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi, the rota shows the same nine people set up and lock up. They are carrying the club.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, exactly. And the quieter members feel uneasy about what their fee covers if they only come twice.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, if we switch to activity-based charging, does that reduce the chasing time?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,Activity-based charging might scare off the newcomers who are already hesitant about commitment.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,It might. But a flat fee ignores the reality that some people use the club heavily and others barely do.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"A tiered system could work, but the minute books from the last time we tried it show friction.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The winter social feedback says people want to belong, not just pay for a ticket.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"We need a balance. We can't afford the admin load of tracking every event, but we can't ignore the inequity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I think a small base fee plus event charges is the most honest, but it risks the turnout drop we saw in summer.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,The summer drop was real. Turnout fell by a third when we tried door charges. We cannot repeat that.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,So we are back to flat or tiered. Tiered feels risky given the past friction.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Flat is safer for the culture, but it feels unfair to the nine who do the work.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Let's vote. I lean toward flat, but I want to hear the final arguments.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
